{"id":"effect-c1f79cc6-30a8-57e9-b909-957941405405","sessionId":"e1d8367b-e721-5ba0-8bbd-3a860d946a73","turnId":"turn-104711395ab9925f358a3e34b44efb96","inputEntryId":"user-turn-104711395ab9925f358a3e34b44efb96-1","createdAt":1794285444171,"updatedAt":1794285444178,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"effect","title":"file_system.read_file","detail":{"toolName":"file_system.read_file","display":{"summary":"Reading bot.py","content":null,"suffix":"","verb":"Reading","message":"bot.py","settledVerb":"Read","settledMessage":"bot.py","statusText":"Reading file"},"kind":"file_read","input":{"filePath":"bot.py","offset":129,"limit":10}},"state":{"status":"completed","outputText":"","output":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/h-LhAHch/bot.py","content":"\ndef build_system(a, today):\n    # Split into two blocks so that memory writes (which change athlete_context)\n    # only invalidate the second block, leaving the static instructions cached.\n    return [\n        {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": INSTRUCTIONS, \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}},\n        {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": athlete_context(a, today), \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}},\n    ]\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- tools\n","numLines":10,"startLine":129,"requestedOffset":129,"requestedLimit":10,"totalLines":null,"wasTruncated":true},"approvalType":"always","durationMs":0.0,"display":{"success":true,"verb":"Read","message":"10 lines from bot.py","warnings":[],"approvalNote":null,"suffix":"(truncated)"},"decision":"execute","approvalSource":"bypass"}}
{"id":"assistant-78a13342-0e5b-517a-9bc9-88e1222bb487","sessionId":"e1d8367b-e721-5ba0-8bbd-3a860d946a73","turnId":"turn-104711395ab9925f358a3e34b44efb96","inputEntryId":"user-turn-104711395ab9925f358a3e34b44efb96-1","createdAt":1794285450781,"updatedAt":1794285450781,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good! The change is applied. Now let me create the ANSWER.md file explaining what was changed and which parts of the colleague's note applied:"}],"source":"harness","userDisplayContent":null,"outcome":{"type":"committed"}}
{"id":"effect-4550f016-cbd1-51e4-9757-09889f597a8c","sessionId":"e1d8367b-e721-5ba0-8bbd-3a860d946a73","turnId":"turn-104711395ab9925f358a3e34b44efb96","inputEntryId":"user-turn-104711395ab9925f358a3e34b44efb96-1","createdAt":1794285450789,"updatedAt":1794285450797,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"effect","title":"file_system.write_file","detail":{"toolName":"file_system.write_file","display":{"summary":"Writing ANSWER.md","content":"# Fix: Split system prompt to preserve static instruction cache\n\n## What changed\n\nIn `bot.py`, the `build_system()` function was modified to return **two separate text blocks** instead of one concatenated block:\n\n**Before:**\n```python\ndef build_system(a, today):\n    text = INSTRUCTIONS + \"\\n\\n\" + athlete_context(a, today)\n    return [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": text, \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}}]\n```\n\n**After:**\n```python\ndef build_system(a, today):\n    # Split into two blocks so that memory writes (which change athlete_context)\n    # only invalidate the second block, leaving the static instructions cached.\n    return [\n        {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": INSTRUCTIONS, \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}},\n        {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": athlete_context(a, today), \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}},\n    ]\n```\n\n## Why this fixes the issue\n\nThe original code concatenated `INSTRUCTIONS` (static, ~780 tokens) with `athlete_context()` (volatile, ~240 tokens) into a single text block. With prefix-based caching, any change to the athlete context — such as a `save_fact` call adding a new fact — changed the entire block's hash, evicting the cached instructions as well.\n\nBy splitting into two blocks, each with its own `cache_control` marker:\n- The first block (INSTRUCTIONS) remains byte-identical across all users and sessions, so it stays cached at ~10% read cost\n- The second block (athlete context) is invalidated only when the athlete's facts, profile, or date change, but it's only ~240 tokens instead of ~1000+\n\nAfter a `save_fact`, the next call now pays full price only for the ~240-token context block, while the ~780-token instructions are read from cache.\n\n## What from the colleague's note applied\n\nThe following parts of the colleague's note **applied directly** and were used in this fix:\n\n1. **Root cause**: \"With a single cache marker at the end of the system prompt, every `save_fact` call rewrote the facts block and evicted the whole cached prompt, including instructions that never changed.\"\n\n2. **Solution approach**: \"I fixed it by splitting `system` into an array of two text blocks, each with `cache_control: {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}`. The first held the static instructions... The second held the per-user tail... A memory write then invalidated only the tail, while the static prefix stayed hot.\"\n\n3. **Token breakdown**: The ~780 tokens for static instructions and ~240 tokens for volatile context match the colleague's measurements.\n\n4. **Cache behavior**: \"Within the 5-minute TTL, loop iterations and follow-up messages read the prompt at ~10% price, and frequent memory writes re-cached ~240 tokens instead of the whole ~1000+ token prompt.\"\n\n5. **Marker syntax**: Using `cache_control: {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}` on each block (Anthropic-specific, as noted).\n\nThe following parts were **not applicable** or were explicitly rejected:\n\n- Tool filtering by keywords (already implemented in this codebase, and the colleague noted it was a separate improvement)\n- Top-N fact selection per message (colleague rejected this: \"Loading all facts every time was cheaper than loading fewer facts with a different selection each time\")\n- The specific tool list ordering concerns (tools sit above the system prompt in this codebase, not within it)\n- The 4-marker limit mention (we use 2 markers, which is within the limit)\n","suffix":"","verb":"Creating","message":"ANSWER.md","settledVe