{"id":"assistant-b0ce94d3-3157-5bda-807d-6ea0a47a87f1","sessionId":"e1d8367b-e721-5ba0-8bbd-3a860d946a73","turnId":"turn-104711395ab9925f358a3e34b44efb96","inputEntryId":"user-turn-104711395ab9925f358a3e34b44efb96-1","createdAt":1794285497871,"updatedAt":1794285497871,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! The task is complete. Let me create a summary of what was done:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed the caching issue in the bot. Here's what was changed:\n\n### Changes Made\n\n**File: `bot.py`**\n- Modified the `build_system()` function to split the system prompt into **two separate text blocks** instead of one concatenated block\n- First block: Static `INSTRUCTIONS` (coaching rules, tone, safety, formatting - ~780 tokens, never changes)\n- Second block: Volatile `athlete_context()` (date, athlete profile, zones, goal, facts, language - ~240 tokens, changes with `save_fact`)\n\n**File: `ANSWER.md`** (created)\n- Documents the exact change made\n- Explains why this fixes the issue (prefix-based caching was evicting the entire prompt when only the context changed)\n- Details which parts of the colleague's note applied and which didn't\n\n### Why This Works\n\nThe original code concatenated static instructions with volatile athlete context into a single cached block. With prefix-based caching, any change (like a `save_fact` adding a new fact) changed the entire block's hash, evicting both the static instructions AND the context from cache.\n\nWith the split:\n- The static instructions block remains byte-identical across all users/sessions → stays cached at ~10% read cost\n- The volatile context block is invalidated only when athlete data changes → only ~240 tokens need to be re-cached instead of ~1000+\n\nAfter a `save_fact`, the next call now pays full price only for the ~240-token context block, while the ~780-token instructions are read from cache at ~10% cost.\n\n### Applied from Colleague's Note\n\n✅ Root cause diagnosis (single cache marker evicting whole prompt)\n✅ Solution approach (split into two blocks with separate cache markers)\n✅ Token breakdown (~780 static + ~240 volatile)\n✅ Cache behavior (10% reads for static, ~240 token re-cache for volatile)\n✅ Marker syntax (`cache_control: {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}`)\n\n❌ Tool filtering (already implemented, separate concern)\n❌ Top-N fact selection (explicitly rejected by colleague)\n❌ Tool ordering concerns (not applicable to this codebase)"}],"source":"harness","userDisplayContent":null,"outcome":{"type":"committed"}}
